From: immortalwrt-x86-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: gso: reject empty fraglist before list segmentation

skb_segment_list() is only valid for SKB_GSO_FRAGLIST packets with a
non-empty frag_list. If the list is missing, it currently returns the head
skb after clearing its list pointer. UDP fraglist completion can then treat
the single skb as a segment list and dereference a missing next segment.

Reject the malformed input before modifying the skb. Valid fraglist GSO and
ordinary GSO paths are unchanged.

This is a defensive Linux 6.6 backport for malformed FM350 receive skbs.

---
 net/core/skbuff.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -4349,4 +4349,7 @@ struct sk_buff *skb_segment_list(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	struct sk_buff *nskb, *tmp;
 	int len_diff, err;
 
+	if (unlikely(!list_skb))
+		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
+
 	/* Only skb_gro_receive_list generated skbs arrive here */
